---
import { Font } from "astro:assets";
import "../styles/global.css";
import "../styles/mathbridge.css";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/")
  ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL
  : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
const live = "https://mathbridge-ai.duckdns.org/";
const projectRepo =
  "https://github.com/jovian-2wang/mathbridge-ai-project-page";
const appRepo = "https://github.com/jovian-2wang/mathbridge-AI";
const award = "https://www.nsf.gov/awardsearch/show-award/?AWD_ID=2627693";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="MathBridge AI is a curriculum-grounded mathematics learning platform for students, teachers, and families."
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={`${base}favicon.svg`} />
    <Font
      cssVariable="--font-noto-sans"
      preload={[{ subset: "latin", style: "normal" }]}
    />
    <title>MathBridge AI | Student-aware mathematics support</title>
  </head>

  <body class="project-page font-(family-name:--font-noto-sans)">
    <header id="top">
      <div class="nav shell">
        <a class="brand" href="#top">MathBridge <b>AI</b></a>
        <nav aria-label="Page navigation">
          <a href="#learning">How it helps</a><a href="#roles">Three views</a><a
            href="#demo">Live demo</a
          ><a href="#pipeline">Research pipeline</a>
        </nav>
      </div>

      <div class="affiliation-band">
        <div class="affiliations shell">
          <div>
            <span>LEAD ORGANIZATION</span><a
              href="https://www.utsa.edu/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              ><img
                src={`${base}brands/ut-san-antonio-logo.svg`}
                alt="The University of Texas at San Antonio"
              /></a
            >
          </div>
          <i aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <div class="uf">
            <span>SUB-AWARDEE ORGANIZATION</span><a
              href="https://www.ufl.edu/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              ><img
                src={`${base}brands/uf-logo-full.png`}
                alt="University of Florida"
              /></a
            >
          </div>
          <a
            class="award-link"
            href={award}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">NSF Award #2627693 ↗</a
          >
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero shell">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="overline">INTERACTIVE RESEARCH PROJECT</p>
          <h1>MathBridge AI</h1>
          <p class="subtitle">
            Stuck on a math problem? Get one helpful clue, then try again.
          </p>
          <p class="summary">
            MathBridge starts with the Math 6 problem from class. It looks at
            the student’s work and helps with the exact step that feels hard.
            Students can choose examples they enjoy, add Chinese or Spanish,
            and listen when reading the question is difficult.
          </p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="primary" href="#demo">Explore the live demo</a><a
              href={live}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">Open platform ↗</a
            ><a href={projectRepo} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Project code ↗</a
            ><a href={award} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >NSF award ↗</a
            >
          </div>
          <p class="private-repo">
            Application source: <a
              href={appRepo}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">private repository ↗</a
            >
          </p>
        </div>

        <aside
          class="hero-example"
          aria-label="Example of student-aware support"
        >
          <div class="task-tag">MATH 6 · UNIT RATE</div>
          <p class="question">
            24 points in 3 games at the same rate. How many points per game?
          </p>
          <div class="attempt">
            <span>YOU TRIED</span><strong>6 points per game</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="diagnosis">
            <span>HERE IS THE STUCK STEP</span><strong
              >6 points for each game would make 18, not 24.</strong
            >
          </div>
          <div class="next-step">
            <span>ONE CLUE</span><strong
              >“Three equal groups make 24. What number times 3 makes 24?”</strong
            >
          </div>
          <div class="retry">GET A CLUE → TRY AGAIN → PRACTICE ONCE MORE</div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section id="learning" class="section pale">
        <div class="shell">
          <div class="section-head">
            <p class="overline">01 / HOW IT HELPS</p><h2>
              You do the thinking. MathBridge helps you keep going.
            </h2>
          </div>
          <div class="core-loop">
            <article class="primary-step">
              <span>1</span><div>
                <small>FROM CLASS</small><h3>Your Math 6 problem</h3>
              </div>
            </article>
            <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
            <article>
              <span>2</span><div>
                <small>FIRST</small><h3>You give it a try</h3>
              </div>
            </article>
            <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
            <article>
              <span>3</span><div>
                <small>THEN</small><h3>We find the stuck step</h3>
              </div>
            </article>
            <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
            <article>
              <span>4</span><div>
                <small>HELP</small><h3>You get one clear clue</h3>
              </div>
            </article>
            <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
            <article class="retry-step">
              <span>5</span><div>
                <small>YOUR TURN</small><h3>You try again</h3>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
          <p class="loop-explanation">
            <b>The class problem always comes first.</b> MathBridge does not
            change the math or give away the answer. It gives just enough help
            for the student to make the next move.
          </p>

          <div class="preference-title">
            <p class="overline">CHOOSE WHAT HELPS YOU LEARN</p><h3>
              The same math can be explained in a way that works better for you.
            </h3>
          </div>
          <div class="preference-grid">
            <article>
              <span>THINGS I LIKE</span><h4>
                Make a clue feel familiar.
              </h4><p>
                Choose basketball, baking, or games. A clue can use that topic
                to explain the hard step. The class problem stays the same.
              </p><div>
                <b>Basketball: points ÷ games</b><em>→ still the same division</em>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span>MY LANGUAGE</span><h4>
                Understand the words and focus on the math.
              </h4><p>
                Keep the English question on screen and add Chinese or Spanish
                underneath. This helps with tricky words without changing the
                math.
              </p><div>
                <b>“unit rate” + 单位率</b><em>→ one idea, two languages</em>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span>READ IT TO ME</span><h4>Listen when reading feels hard.</h4><p>
                Press play to hear the question or clue. Nothing plays by
                surprise, and the student still works out the answer.
              </p><div>
                <b>Press play when you want</b><em>→ no surprise sound</em>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="roles" class="section">
        <div class="shell">
          <div class="section-head">
            <p class="overline">
              02 / ONE PLATFORM, THREE PEOPLE
            </p><h2>Everyone sees what they need—not a wall of data.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="role-grid">
            <article>
              <div class="role-name">STUDENT</div><h3>
                “How do I get unstuck?”
              </h3><div class="role-flow">
                <span>I try</span><b>→</b><span>I get one clue</span><b
                  >→</b
                ><span>Try again</span>
              </div><p>
                The clue helps with the hard step without showing the answer.
              </p><strong class="benefit"
                >The student stays in charge of the thinking.</strong
              >
            </article>
            <article>
              <div class="role-name">TEACHER</div><h3>
                “Where does my class need help?”
              </h3><div class="role-flow">
                <span>See student work</span><b>→</b><span
                  >Spot a common stuck step</span
                ><b>→</b><span>Plan the next lesson</span>
              </div><p>
                The teacher can see which idea is causing trouble and which
                students may need the same kind of help.
              </p><strong class="benefit"
                >Less guessing. More focused small groups and mini-lessons.</strong
              >
            </article>
            <article>
              <div class="role-name">FAMILY</div><h3>
                “What can we work on together?”
              </h3><div class="role-flow">
                <span>See the skill</span><b>→</b><span
                  >Ask one helpful question</span
                ><b>→</b><span>Practice together</span>
              </div><p>
                Families get a short, plain-language update—not a technical
                school report.
              </p><strong class="benefit"
                >A useful 10-minute conversation instead of extra homework.</strong
              >
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="demo" class="section demo-section">
        <div class="shell">
          <div class="split-head">
            <div>
              <p class="overline">03 / LIVE PLATFORM</p><h2>
                Open the real student, teacher, and family views.
              </h2>
            </div><p>
              Choose who you are. The guide shows what that person can do in
              the working platform.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div id="live-demo" class="mb-live">
            <div class="mb-live-head">
              <div class="mb-role-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Choose a MathBridge view">
                <button type="button" role="tab" data-role="student" aria-selected="true">Student</button>
                <button type="button" role="tab" data-role="teacher" aria-selected="false">Teacher</button>
                <button type="button" role="tab" data-role="family" aria-selected="false">Family</button>
              </div>
              <span class="mb-live-label">● WORKING DEMO</span>
            </div>
            <div class="mb-live-grid">
              <aside class="mb-guide">
                <span class="mb-eyebrow">WHAT YOU CAN DO</span>
                <h3 id="demo-guide-title">Practice one step at a time.</h3>
                <p id="demo-guide-intro">Try a class problem. If you get stuck, ask for one clue and try again.</p>
                <ol id="demo-guide-steps">
                  <li>Choose your language, interests, and reading help.</li>
                  <li>Try today’s Math 6 problem.</li>
                  <li>Ask for a clue or picture when you need it.</li>
                </ol>
                <p id="demo-guide-access" class="mb-access">Open the demo and choose Student.</p>
                <a class="mb-open-app" href={live} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the full platform ↗</a>
              </aside>
              <div class="mb-app-window">
                <div class="mb-address"><span aria-hidden="true">● ● ●</span><span>mathbridge-ai.duckdns.org</span><a href={live} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open ↗</a></div>
                <iframe src={live} title="Working MathBridge AI platform" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allow="clipboard-read; clipboard-write"></iframe>
                <div class="mb-app-foot">This is the real working demo. If it does not appear here, <a href={live} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">open it in a new tab ↗</a></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <script is:inline>
            (() => {
              const root = document.getElementById("live-demo");
              if (!root) return;
              const views = {
                student: {
                  title: "Practice one step at a time.",
                  intro: "Try a class problem. If you get stuck, ask for one clue and try again.",
                  steps: ["Choose your language, interests, and reading help.", "Try today’s Math 6 problem.", "Ask for a clue or picture when you need it."],
                  access: "Open the demo and choose Student."
                },
                teacher: {
                  title: "See where students got stuck.",
                  intro: "Look beyond right or wrong. See the step that needs another explanation.",
                  steps: ["See recent student attempts.", "Find students stuck on the same idea.", "Plan a small group or short mini-lesson."],
                  access: "Open the demo and choose Teacher."
                },
                family: {
                  title: "Know how to help at home.",
                  intro: "Get a short update, one question to ask, and a quick activity to try together.",
                  steps: ["See what your child is learning.", "Read one helpful question to ask.", "Try a short practice problem together."],
                  access: "Open the demo and choose Parent."
                }
              };
              const buttons = [...root.querySelectorAll("[data-role]")];
              buttons.forEach((button) => button.addEventListener("click", () => {
                const view = views[button.dataset.role];
                root.querySelector("#demo-guide-title").textContent = view.title;
                root.querySelector("#demo-guide-intro").textContent = view.intro;
                root.querySelector("#demo-guide-access").textContent = view.access;
                root.querySelector("#demo-guide-steps").replaceChildren(...view.steps.map((step) => {
                  const item = document.createElement("li");
                  item.textContent = step;
                  return item;
                }));
                buttons.forEach((item) => item.setAttribute("aria-selected", String(item === button)));
              }));
            })();
          </script>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section preference-demo">
        <div class="shell">
          <div class="split-head">
            <div>
              <p class="overline">04 / TRY THE PREFERENCE LOGIC</p><h2>
                Try it: make the help feel like yours.
              </h2>
            </div><p>
              Change the topic, add a translation, or turn on the play button.
              Then solve the problem and ask for a clue if you need one.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div id="learning-lab" class="mb-lab">
            <div class="mb-profile">
              <span class="mb-eyebrow">MY CHOICES</span>
              <h3>Make the help work for you.</h3>
              <p>Try these buttons. They change the clue—not the class problem.</p>
              <fieldset>
                <legend>Add a translation</legend>
                <div class="mb-chips">
                  <button type="button" data-lang="en" aria-pressed="true">English</button>
                  <button type="button" data-lang="zh" aria-pressed="false">English + 中文</button>
                  <button type="button" data-lang="es" aria-pressed="false">English + Español</button>
                </div>
              </fieldset>
              <fieldset>
                <legend>Things I like <small>— used inside the clue</small></legend>
                <div class="mb-chips">
                  <button type="button" data-interest="basketball" aria-pressed="true">Basketball</button>
                  <button type="button" data-interest="baking" aria-pressed="false">Baking</button>
                  <button type="button" data-interest="games" aria-pressed="false">Games</button>
                </div>
              </fieldset>
              <label class="mb-audio-setting">
                <input id="lab-audio" type="checkbox" />
                <span><strong>Show the play button</strong><small>Sound starts only when you press Play</small></span>
              </label>
              <div class="mb-constant">
                <small>THE CLASS PROBLEM NEVER CHANGES</small>
                <strong id="lab-constant">24 ÷ 3 = ?</strong>
                <span>Your choices only change how the clue is explained.</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="mb-example">
              <div class="mb-example-bar"><span>MATH 6 / TRY IT</span><span id="lab-round">01 / 02</span></div>
              <div class="mb-example-body">
                <span class="mb-topic">YOUR CLASS PROBLEM</span>
                <h3 id="lab-question">A class packs 24 notebooks equally into 3 boxes. How many notebooks go in each box?</h3>
                <p id="lab-translation" class="mb-translation" hidden></p>
                <button id="lab-listen" class="mb-listen" type="button" hidden>▶ Play the question</button>
                <form id="lab-form">
                  <label for="lab-answer">Your answer</label>
                  <div class="mb-answer-row"><input id="lab-answer" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" type="text" /><span id="lab-unit">notebooks in each box</span><button type="submit">Check</button></div>
                </form>
                <p id="lab-feedback" class="mb-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
                <div class="mb-help-buttons"><button id="lab-hint" type="button">Give me one clue</button><button id="lab-visual" type="button">Show a picture ▦</button></div>
                <div id="lab-hint-panel" class="mb-help-panel" hidden><span>YOUR CLUE</span><p id="lab-hint-copy"></p><p id="lab-hint-second" hidden></p><button id="lab-hint-listen" class="mb-listen" type="button" hidden>▶ Play the clue</button></div>
                <div id="lab-ratio-panel" class="mb-ratio-panel" hidden>
                  <span>SHARE THE NOTEBOOKS EQUALLY</span>
                  <table aria-label="Equal groups table"><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Boxes</th><td>1</td><td>2</td><td id="lab-boxes">3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Notebooks</th><td>?</td><td>?</td><td id="lab-total">24</td></tr></tbody></table>
                  <p>What number belongs under 1 box?</p>
                </div>
                <button id="lab-next" class="mb-next" type="button" hidden>Try one more →</button>
              </div>
              <div class="mb-example-foot"><span>TRY → GET ONE CLUE → TRY AGAIN</span><a href="#demo">Open the full demo ↘</a></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <script is:inline>
            (() => {
              const root = document.getElementById("learning-lab");
              if (!root) return;
              const get = (selector) => root.querySelector(selector);
              const questions = [
                "A class packs 24 notebooks equally into 3 boxes. How many notebooks go in each box?",
                "A class packs 36 markers equally into 4 bins. How many markers go in each bin?"
              ];
              const translations = {
                zh: ["一个班把 24 本练习册平均装进 3 个箱子。每个箱子里有多少本？", "一个班把 36 支彩笔平均放进 4 个盒子。每个盒子里有多少支？"],
                es: ["Una clase reparte 24 cuadernos por igual en 3 cajas. ¿Cuántos van en cada caja?", "Una clase reparte 36 marcadores por igual en 4 recipientes. ¿Cuántos van en cada uno?"]
              };
              const clues = {
                basketball: ["Think about 24 points shared across 3 games. How many points would go with one game? Use that same division here.", "Think about 36 points shared across 4 games. How many points would go with one game?"],
                baking: ["Think about 24 cookies shared across 3 trays. How many cookies would go on one tray? Use that same division here.", "Think about 36 cookies shared across 4 trays. How many cookies would go on one tray?"],
                games: ["Think about 24 coins shared across 3 game levels. How many coins would go in one level? Use that same division here.", "Think about 36 coins shared across 4 levels. How many coins would go in one level?"]
              };
              let lang = "en";
              let interest = "basketball";
              let round = 0;
              const answer = get("#lab-answer");
              const audio = get("#lab-audio");
              const speak = (words) => {
                if (!("speechSynthesis" in window)) return;
                window.speechSynthesis.cancel();
                const voiceLine = new SpeechSynthesisUtterance(words);
                const voices = window.speechSynthesis.getVoices();
                voiceLine.voice = voices.find((voice) => /Samantha|Google US English|Microsoft Aria|Ava|Karen/i.test(voice.name)) || voices.find((voice) => voice.lang === "en-US") || null;
                voiceLine.lang = "en-US";
                voiceLine.rate = 0.92;
                voiceLine.pitch = 1;
                voiceLine.volume = 0.85;
                window.speechSynthesis.speak(voiceLine);
              };
              const draw = () => {
                get("#lab-question").textContent = questions[round];
                get("#lab-constant").textContent = round ? "36 ÷ 4 = ?" : "24 ÷ 3 = ?";
                get("#lab-unit").textContent = round ? "markers in each bin" : "notebooks in each box";
                get("#lab-round").textContent = round ? "02 / 02" : "01 / 02";
                get("#lab-boxes").textContent = round ? "4" : "3";
                get("#lab-total").textContent = round ? "36" : "24";
                const translation = get("#lab-translation");
                translation.hidden = lang === "en";
                translation.textContent = lang === "en" ? "" : translations[lang][round];
                get("#lab-hint-copy").textContent = clues[interest][round];
                const second = get("#lab-hint-second");
                second.hidden = lang === "en";
                second.textContent = lang === "zh" ? (round ? "想一想：36 平均分成 4 份，每份是多少？" : "想一想：24 平均分成 3 份，每份是多少？") : (lang === "es" ? (round ? "Piensa: si repartes 36 en 4 grupos iguales, ¿cuánto hay en cada grupo?" : "Piensa: si repartes 24 en 3 grupos iguales, ¿cuánto hay en cada grupo?") : "");
                get("#lab-listen").hidden = !audio.checked;
                get("#lab-hint-listen").hidden = !audio.checked;
                get("#lab-hint-panel").hidden = true;
                get("#lab-ratio-panel").hidden = true;
                get("#lab-next").hidden = true;
                get("#lab-feedback").textContent = "";
                get("#lab-feedback").className = "mb-feedback";
                answer.value = "";
                root.querySelectorAll("[data-lang]").forEach((button) => button.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(button.dataset.lang === lang)));
                root.querySelectorAll("[data-interest]").forEach((button) => button.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(button.dataset.interest === interest)));
              };
              root.querySelectorAll("[data-lang]").forEach((button) => button.addEventListener("click", () => { lang = button.dataset.lang; draw(); }));
              root.querySelectorAll("[data-interest]").forEach((button) => button.addEventListener("click", () => { interest = button.dataset.interest; get("#lab-hint-copy").textContent = clues[interest][round]; }));
              audio.addEventListener("change", () => {
                get("#lab-listen").hidden = !audio.checked;
                get("#lab-hint-listen").hidden = !audio.checked;
                if (!audio.checked && "speechSynthesis" in window) window.speechSynthesis.cancel();
              });
              get("#lab-listen").addEventListener("click", () => speak(questions[round]));
              get("#lab-hint-listen").addEventListener("click", () => speak(clues[interest][round]));
              get("#lab-hint").addEventListener("click", () => { get("#lab-hint-copy").textContent = clues[interest][round]; get("#lab-hint-panel").hidden = false; });
              get("#lab-visual").addEventListener("click", () => { get("#lab-ratio-panel").hidden = false; });
              get("#lab-next").addEventListener("click", () => { round = 1; draw(); answer.focus(); });
              get("#lab-form").addEventListener("submit", (event) => {
                event.preventDefault();
                const feedback = get("#lab-feedback");
                if (!answer.value.trim()) { feedback.textContent = "Type a number first."; answer.focus(); return; }
                if (Number(answer.value) === (round ? 9 : 8)) {
                  feedback.textContent = round ? "Yes—9 is right. You used the same idea again!" : "Yes—8 is right. Now try the same idea one more time.";
                  feedback.classList.add("is-correct");
                  get("#lab-next").hidden = Boolean(round);
                } else {
                  feedback.textContent = "Not yet. Open one clue or the picture, then try again.";
                }
              });
              draw();
            })();
          </script>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="pipeline" class="section pipeline-section">
        <div class="shell">
          <div class="section-head">
            <p class="overline">05 / HOW THE SUPPORT IS BUILT</p><h2>
              The Student Edition leads. The Answer Edition only helps check the support.
            </h2><p>
              There are two separate jobs: prepare helpful material before
              students arrive, then use it only when a student needs a clue.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="pipeline-stack">
            <section class="pipeline-block">
              <header>
                <span>BEFORE STUDENTS USE IT</span><h3>
                  Build and check the help.
                </h3>
              </header>
              <div class="primary-route">
                <div>
                  <small>THE COURSE</small><strong
                    >Math 6 Student Edition task</strong>
                </div><b>→</b><div>
                  <small>WHAT STUDENTS LEARN</small><strong
                    >Problem + math skill</strong>
                </div><b>→</b><div class="database-box">
                  <small>SAVED FOR THE PLATFORM</small><strong
                    >Course task and checked support</strong>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="aux-route">
                <span>USED TO CHECK</span><div>
                  <small>Math 6 Answer Edition</small><strong
                    >Correct answer + worked solution</strong>
                </div><b>→</b><div>
                  <small>Automatic review</small><strong
                    >Keep accurate explanations</strong>
                </div><b>↗</b>
              </div>
              <p class="pipeline-note">
                The Answer Edition checks accuracy. It never replaces the
                Student Edition task and is never copied to the student as a clue.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section class="pipeline-block">
              <header>
                <span>WHILE A STUDENT IS PRACTICING</span><h3>
                  Start with the student’s own work.
                </h3>
              </header>
              <div class="runtime-route">
                <div><small>COURSE</small><strong>Math 6 task</strong></div><b
                  >→</b
